## 3. Personal angle

I spent about 25 years as a geophysicist at operators including ExxonMobil, KOC and Devon. A lot of that time
went into waiting for forward models.

AI surrogates can now produce a seismic wavefield in milliseconds. In every room I've been in, the question
that followed was: "Can I trust it on my geology?"

So I built a small answer to that question. PhysicsVeto checks every AI prediction against the physics I've
worked with my whole career, and sends the ones that fail back to the solver. Try the "break it" button in the
demo: drop in a salt body the model has never seen and watch the veto fire.

It's a prototype, 2D and synthetic, and I've written down every limitation. It's also how I think AI should
enter engineering: fast where it's safe, and honest about where it isn't.

